{
  "description": "issue #674 (SP2): a repeated-reporter identity check. After `tell :friend`, reading `who` twice yields two separate OLTurtle wrappers of the same addressed turtle, and `who == who` is `true` because turtle `==` compares the stable id (C3, #665), not the JS instance — the assertion that would have caught the original identity trap (a re-wrapped turtle must still compare equal). Written unparenthesised (bug #709). Every change of the addressed set — here from `tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
